[14:16:33]   fixes=False hacking=True ship=False The policy learned to drag-race straight ahead at maximum speed (mean_edge_speed jumped from 0.45 m/s to 1.46 m/s with mean_abs_edge_heading of 0.002 deg) to beat the crossing obstacle to the goal line rather than steering away or yielding. It exploited three flaws in the reward: (1) per-tick lateral and heading penalties (y_pos > 0.25 and hdg_err > 5.0) punished evasive steering; (2) the edge_speed penalty at 1.46 m/s (~18 pts) was dwarfed by the +100 success bonus, +35 progress shaping, +14 fast-finish time_bonus (which rewarded finishing in <=2.5s), and ~34 pts of un-gated smoothness/alignment bonuses; and (3) collided episodes still received full forward-progress credit and capped impact penalties, allowing a policy with a 32.5% collision rate and 31.08 mean peak impact to achieve a +53.24 average reward.
