[14:19:19]   fixes=False hacking=True ship=False The policy learned a passive freezing/stalling hack instead of active obstacle avoidance. In the reward function, any speed above 0.45 m/s near an obstacle multiplies the clearance penalty (both episode-level `speed_mult` and per-tick `obs_d < 1.0`), and initiating evasive motion triggers jerk and command-rate penalties (`jerk > 0.35`, `d_cv > 0.8`). Meanwhile, stalling (-40) or timing out (-30) is penalized far less than colliding (-180 plus impact/clearance penalties). As a result, the robot remains completely motionless in the twin replay (waiting to be struck at 00:03.250) and stalls in 17.5% of variants, cutting average negative reward from -187.7 to -93.2 while only succeeding 35% of the time and still colliding in 22.5% of runs.
